00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:06.095
Problem 33 asks: What distance
did Jane travel?

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:13.440
What distance did she travel?

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.790
So, one.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:26.250
Bill traveled 40 miles in 40
minutes, or essentially a mile

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.980
a minute, which is 60 miles an
hour, whatever, 1 mile a

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.380
minute, right?

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.180
That's what we can figure out.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.680
1 mile per minute.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.420
That has no information about
how far did Jane travel.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.200
It's useless.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.500
Two.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.070
Jane traveled at the same
average rate as Bill.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:48.590
So that tells that Jane, if she
went at the same average

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.900
rate as Bill, that means
that she also

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.180
went 1 mile per minute.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:57.030
But we're not asking for how
fast did Jane travel or what

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.220
was her average rate.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.700
We're asking for how
far did she travel?

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.110
So with statements one and two
combined, all we know is

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.850
Jane's rate, but we don't know
how long she traveled for.

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:08.870
So we don't know the distance.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:12.310
So the answer is e, that both
statements together are not

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:12.790
sufficient.

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:16.800
If statement two told us that
Jane traveled at the same rate

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.440
as Bill and she traveled at that
rate for 10 minutes, then

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.470
we would be able to solve
this problem.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:25.910
But it didn't, so even with both
pieces of information, we

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.705
still don't know how far
Jane traveled, only

00:01:28.705 --> 00:01:30.330
how fast she traveled.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:31.420
34.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:36.760
What number is 15% of x?

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:42.100
So what we want to
know is 0.15x.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.910
That's what we're trying
to solve for.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:55.530
Statement one tells
us, 18 is 6% of x.

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.580
So you normally wouldn't even
have to solve for it.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:00.370
All you know is, by looking
at this statement, you

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.690
can solve for x.

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.390
And if you can solve for x,
then you can just multiply

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.910
that times 0.15, and you'll
have the answer to the

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:07.920
original statement.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.750
So you immediately know that
statement one is sufficient.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.370
If you don't believe
me, you can just

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:14.510
write this as a equation.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:18.940
18 is equal to 6% of x.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:20.535
And then you just solve for x.

00:02:20.535 --> 00:02:24.120
So 18 divided by 0.06, and then
multiply it times 0.15,

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.370
and you've got your answer.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:30.340
Statement number two.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:35.650
2/3 of x is 200.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:38.200
Once again, you look at
this, and you say,

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.630
this is a simple equation.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.120
I could solve for x.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.010
If I solve for x here, then I
just substitute it back here,

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:48.450
and I will know what 15% of
x is, and I would be done.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:52.100
So each of these statements
individually are sufficient to

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:59.560
answer our question
what is 15% of x.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.930
I don't think I've got to go
through the exercise of

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.710
actually solving for that,
because I think you understand

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:04.460
what I'm talking about.

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:05.750
35.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:06.760
Oh, I like these.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:17.550
So they say 3.2 rectangle
triangle, or delta, 6.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.940
And they say, if rectangle and
delta, or triangle, soon. each

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:24.560
represent single digits
in the decimal above.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:24.820
OK.

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:25.550
So this is a decimal.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:26.860
I thought they might
be operations.

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:27.630
So this is a decimal.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:31.410
So it's four digits behind
the decimal spot.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:34.115
What does rectangle represent?

00:03:34.115 --> 00:03:36.910
So we want to know what does
this decimal-- what's the

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:39.440
digit right here?

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:43.410
Statement number one tells us,
when the decimal is rounded to

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:47.480
the nearest tenth, 3.2
is the result.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.140
The nearest tenth.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:51.250
So when you round, what you do
is you look at-- if we're

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:55.020
rounding to the nearest tenth,
we look at this number, right?

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:56.360
We look at the rectangle.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:01.036
And if the rectangle is 5 or
greater, we would round up, so

00:04:01.036 --> 00:04:02.520
we would get to 3.3.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:06.750
If the rectangle is less
than 5, then we would

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:09.070
round down to 2.

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:14.880
So statement number one tells
us that rectangle

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.769
is less than 5.

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:19.220
And we know it's greater
than or equal to 0,

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.040
because it's a digit.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.650
It's 0, 1, 2, 3, or 4, right?

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:26.410
So we can say it's
0, 1, 2, 3, or 4.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:27.010
That's rectangle.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:29.420
But that by itself does not
allow to figure out what

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.040
rectangle is.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:37.420
Now statement number two tells
us, when the decimal is

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:43.940
rounded to the nearest
hundredth, 3.24 is the result.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:46.910
3.24 is the result
when you round

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:50.010
to the nearest hundredth.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:50.340
OK.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:53.340
So this is interesting.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:59.090
So this number here is either
going to be-- so when you're

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:01.180
rounding to something, it's
either going to be either

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:02.830
rounding down or rounding up.

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:07.470
So this tells us-- so this
number right here can either

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:14.130
be 3-- so we already know, it
can be 0, 1, 2, 3, or 4.

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:18.060
But which of these numbers when
you round them could be

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:21.520
rounded up or down to 4?

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:28.830
Well, this could be
2, 3, 5, right?

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:30.780
Let me give you one scenario.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:40.430
We could have 3.2356, where this
is the rectangle and this

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:41.660
is triangle.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:44.690
So this would round to 3.24.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:52.630
You could also have 3.2416.

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:57.040
where this is the rectangle
and this is the triangle.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:00.510
And either of these would
round to 3.24.

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:04.450
So this tells us essentially
that the rectangle has to be

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:05.710
either 3 or 4.

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:16.400
And this tells us that it's
either 0, 1, 2, 3, or 4.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.670
But even when you use them
individually, they don't tell

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:20.490
you exactly what the
rectangle is.

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:22.340
And when you use them together,
you can just narrow

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:25.380
down to 3 or 4, which just
statement two alone tells you.

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:27.460
So this actually turns out
that when you use both

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.670
statements together, you still
can't get the answer.

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:32.810
You'd either need a third term
there, or we would have to

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:34.490
have a little bit more
information about what the

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.520
triangle is.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:41.230
If they told us that the
triangle rounds you up or is

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:43.590
greater than 5 or less than 5
or something like that, then

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:46.400
we could figure out what
the rectangle is.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.220
So they answer here is E, if
I haven't missed something.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:52.340
That together, both statements
are not sufficient to answer

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:53.590
the question.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:57.480
36.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:01.790
A profit from the sale of a
certain appliance increases,

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:04.600
though not proportionally with
the number of units sold.

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:13.950
So it's not-- you know, the
profits do not equal just some

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.150
constant times units.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:19.060
It equals maybe some constant
times units squared or

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:20.910
something like that.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:23.290
Did the profit exceed
4 million on

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:26.360
sales of 380,000 units?

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:31.440
So is profit greater than
4 million-- this one is

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:41.080
interesting-- when units
is equal to 380,000?

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:44.150
Let's see if we can
figure this out.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:47.110
So they say that the
profit exceeds 2

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:50.890
million on sales of 200,000.

00:07:50.890 --> 00:07:56.460
So statement one says profit is
greater than 2 million when

00:07:56.460 --> 00:08:00.890
units is equal to 200,000.

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:04.760
Now, if they told us that profit
was proportional to

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:10.150
units, then we could say, oh,
well, if we increase the units

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:13.790
from 200,000 to 380,000, then
we're not doubling the units.

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:17.640
So then we can't be-- well, it
still would be ambiguous

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.260
because they're not saying
profit equals 2.

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:21.560
They're saying that profit is
greater than 2, so this

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:24.110
actually still doesn't give
me a lot of information.

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:25.770
Statement number two.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.170
I'll do it in a different
color.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:32.190
Statement number two says the
profit exceeds 5 million on

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:45.220
sales of 350,000 units.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:45.660
OK.

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.390
So this is interesting.

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:51.550
So this tells us that when units
are 350,000, our profit

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:54.970
is already greater than 5
million, so they're definitely

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:56.340
greater than 4 million.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:09:00.580
And notice, they told us that
the profit from the sale of an

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:03.220
appliance increases, but not
proportionally, with the

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:04.240
number of units sold.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:08.980
So if we made more than 5
million when there are 350,000

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:13.130
units, we know that when you go
from 350,000 to 380,000, we

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:15.570
know from the statement of
the problem that the

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:16.800
profit has to increase.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:19.540
We don't know by how much, but
it's going to increase.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:21.955
So the profit was already
greater than 5 million.

00:09:21.955 --> 00:09:24.630
It's going to increase
above 5 million.

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:27.130
So statement two tells us that
the profit is definitely going

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:28.700
to be above 5 million, so
it's definitely going

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.290
to be above 4 million.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:34.350
So statement two alone
is enough.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:36.550
And statement one actually
tells us very little

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.420
information because we don't
know how does the profit

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:42.100
change as you incrementally
add units.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:46.040
Maybe every other unit-- maybe
every unit above 200,000 that

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:48.400
you add, you get, a millionth
of a penny.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:49.700
And then it doesn't
tell you anything.

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:51.340
Or maybe you get a
million pennies.

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:53.470
So it's very hard to tell.

